Multiplier utilization = useful MACs / (multipliers x clocks)
  useful MACs = 32 candidates x H steps x 80 network MACs (48 layer 1 + 32 layer 2)
  multipliers = LANES (one per lane); clocks = measured clocks per decision
  'busy' also counts the 3 cost squares per step, which use the same multiplier

  LANES   H  multipliers  clocks  useful MACs  mult-clocks  utilization    busy
     32  15           32    1281        38400        40992       93.68%  97.19%
     16  15           16    2528        38400        40448       94.94%  98.50%
      8  15            8    5022        38400        40176       95.58%  99.16%
     32   5           32     451        12800        14432       88.69%  92.02%
     16   5           16     868        12800        13888       92.17%  95.62%
      8   5            8    1702        12800        13616       94.01%  97.53%
  The multipliers sit idle in INIT and STORE (2 clocks per pass) and in DRAIN, ARG
  and DONE (34 clocks per decision). Fewer lanes means more passes over the same
  34-clock tail, so utilization goes up as LANES goes down, even though each
  decision takes longer.

